  "query_preview": "..\n(Friday night through Wednesday)\nIssued at 1256 AM CST Thu Nov 5 2026\n\nA second low quickly replaces the first, dropping to the\nAZ/NM/Mexico border Saturday. Models have been trending stronger\nand deeper with this low, now showing it cutting off over northern\nMexico and causing good rain chances mainly south of I-20 though\nmore isolated showers could be seen as far north as Seminole,\nLamesa, and Snyder. The deep low will pull some gulf moisture \nback west, but the moisture is still limited and rainfall amounts\nwill mostly be less than a quarter of an inch this weekend. \n\nModels continue to show the upper pattern next week will be zonal\nwith a split jet, the southern stream oriented over West Texas and\nsouthern New Mexico. This effectively cuts our CWA off from cold\nCanadian air but also prevents ridging that would increase temps\nmuch. So the extended temperature forecast is near normal. There\nmay be another disturbance next week moving through in the\nsouthern jet stream and a few deterministic models are showing\nisolated showers associated with it next week. There are not\nenough models showing the precip for it to show in the NBM\nforecast at this time.\n\nHennig",
